Appendix D. Stochastic Optimal Control: FBSDE and Reinforcement Learning

D.1 Full FBSDE Formulation

The optimal harvesting problem can be cast as a forward–backward stochastic differential equation (FBSDE) using the stochastic maximum principle. Define the Hamiltonian:

\mathcal{H}(t,Y,S,\theta,p_Y,p_S,q_Y) = u(c) + p_Y \mu_A Y + p_S[(r^S-\phi)S + \theta Y - D] + q_Y \sigma_A Y,

where p_Y,p_S are co-states and q_Y the diffusion co-state for Y. The optimal \theta satisfies \partial \mathcal{H}/\partial\theta = 0 → u'(c) = p_S. The adjoint equations:

dp_Y = -\frac{\partial\mathcal{H}}{\partial Y} dt + q_Y dW, \qquad p_Y(T)=0 \text{ (or transversality)},

dp_S = -\frac{\partial\mathcal{H}}{\partial S} dt.

Under CRRA, the FBSDE can be linearised around the steady state and solved using the deep learning method of Han & Long (2020) for high-dimensional FBSDEs.

D.2 Reinforcement Learning Algorithm (Pseudocode)

```
Initialize Q-network (critic) and policy network (actor) for θ(S,Y)
For episode = 1 to M:
    Reset state: Y ~ initial distribution, S = S0
    For t = 0 to T:
        Observe (Y_t, S_t)
        Sample θ_t from policy π(·|Y_t,S_t)
        Compute pension outflow O_t = R_t b_t
        Compute D_t = φ S_t, contribution C_t = θ_t Y_t
        If C_t + D_t < O_t: deficit penalty (terminal)
        Next state: Y_{t+1} ~ transition(Y_t,θ_t), S_{t+1}= (1+r^S-φ)S_t + C_t - D_t
        Reward: u(Y_t + (r^S-φ)S_t - C_t) - penalty * max(0, O_t - C_t - D_t)^2
        Store transition in replay buffer
        Update actor-critic using TD error
    End for
End for
```

The algorithm incorporates model uncertainty by randomising transition parameters (μ_A, σ_A, jump intensity) and learns a robust policy, consistent with the OPTCON2 passive learning approach (2f3b).

