Appendix G. Robustness Checks

· Alternative production functions: All main theorems recomputed under a Cobb-Douglas (\sigma=1) and a Leontief (\sigma\to0) limit. Only the \sigma>1 case ensures long-run sustainability without perpetual increases in \tau.
· Endogenous retirement age: If the retirement age adjusts to demographic shifts, the growth rate g_R declines, relaxing condition C1. Simulations with an endogenous rule (linking retirement age to life expectancy) show that PSI paths remain positive even under moderate AI growth.
· Open economy extension: In a two-country model with mobile AI capital, a higher domestic APC induces capital flight unless coordinated. A Nash equilibrium shows that the uncoordinated outcome results in a suboptimally low global APC (proof available upon request).

